WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk about
certainly another thing,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
give you a chance to clarify,
the Green New Deal.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-One of the things we're even

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
hearing the president say
is that you would outlaw cows.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Cows farting.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:14.547
That's would be out -- children,
hamburgers, ice cream.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.116 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Any of that true at all?

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. In fact, I think it is
interesting.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's always good to see how
these narratives

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
are manipulated, because
they're trying to say

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.396
that the Green New Deal is about
what we have to give up,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.730 line:92%
what we have to cut back on,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
when, in fact,
the Green New Deal itself

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a resolution
to be more expansive.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is to be able to
generate more

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to make sure that we're
investing

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.842 line:92%
in working-class Americans

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that we all can afford
to have more in life.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
So an affordable apartment
isn't a dream,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:52.986
but a norm and that healthcare
is a right, not a privilege.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:56.589 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.589 --> 00:01:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, honestly, the only reason
I think anyone would have

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.696
to cut back on ice cream is
if their doctor advised them to.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.132 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah. And sometimes
doctors will do that.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:10.336
Also it should be pointed out,
though, there are some Democrats

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.971 line:92%
who seem a little cautious

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how ambitious
the Green New Deal is.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you talk
to your colleagues

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
within your own party
to let them know

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this is the right path
to take?

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.483
And have you met with
a lot of interparty resistance?

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, I think one
of the things that's important

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
that doesn't get communicated
is that

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
our Green New Deal legislation
is not a bill.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a resolution.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there's two different kinds
of legislation,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what a resolution does
is that if we pass

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:40.900 line:92%
the resolution in the House,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.968 line:92%
it doesn't go into the Senate,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it doesn't go to
the president.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.972 line:92%
It is a House resolution.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:46.773 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It is a declaration.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is an intentional
vision document.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.880
And what it does is that it
puts forward the large scope,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.850
the overall vision of what
we're trying to accomplish,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.353
and to say, listen,
if we're going to make progress,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
we need to declare
our North Star

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our North Star
is 100% renewable energy,

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:05.825 size:81% position:41% line:92%
it's Medicare for all,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's tuition-free
public colleges,

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's investing in technology
and renewable --

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
renewable resources
and electric vehicles.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.871 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And -- and as a result,

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:23.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
any legislation, any actual
bills that do follow from that

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are pieces of that.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:29.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can have one bill
that just addresses, you know,

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:34.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
battery storage,
like Representative Takano

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:34.754 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
out in California.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can have bills
that just address

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.659 line:92%
infrastructure investment.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so,
all of those are pieces,

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the resolution
of the Green New Deal

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:47.400
is the vision of what we need to
accomplish in the next 10 years.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.101 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It's really exciting.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:51.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I hope people actually
look at what it says.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.772 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.476
Another thing that I think
everyone is appreciating

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:59.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this new generation
of people that are in Congress

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.247
is that it strikes me
that people show up in Congress

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.583
and then people who've been
there longer said to them,

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, this is how
it works here."

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.253
And it seems like a lot of you
are now doing us the service

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
of turning to us and going,
like,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You guys won't believe
how it works here,"

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.692
and telling us as opposed to
just accepting these rules.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You posted this photo,
which was fascinating to me.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Explain what's going on here
real quick.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.234 line:92%
-So I was shocked at this photo.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
What this photo represents
are folks

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are experiencing
homelessness

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.976 line:92%
that have been paid by lobbyists

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
to wait outside
of committee rooms

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that lobbyists can be
the first

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.650
and oftentimes only seats
in a congressional hearing.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're basically holding
a place in line?

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.
-And when you saw that,

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.957 size:84% position:42%
this has been happening
for a very long time.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I certainly never heard
of it,

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:48.294
and I appreciate you
putting it out on social media,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think
it's a helpful thing for us

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.998
to know exactly what's going on
in this hall of this building

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:52.865 line:92%
that we're all chipping in for.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:56.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's not to say
that these folks sitting down

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:56.869 line:92%
are doing anything wrong.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
Congressional hearings

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
are not a Beyoncé concert,
you know?

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-They're two different things.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is one way in which
money and politics

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:11.317
has really sunk so steep
to the fact that everyday people

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.386
can't even see their own elected
officials

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
because a lobbyist has paid
to get in there first.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to point out
one more thing

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:22.061
on the Green New Deal before
we go because the president said

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.730 line:92%
it was, like, a bad report.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was a poorly written --

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did not buy the science
in it.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.002 size:81% position:41%
But it's very unfair
to say that about you.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are a winner
of science awards.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Look at that.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:36.142 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I personally never
went past, like,

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:47.086
the papier-mââché volcano that my
dad definitely made and not me.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:47.620 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.155 line:92%
But this was a passion of yours

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were in high school,
right?

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah,
science was my first passion.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:56.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I pursued
the Intel science competition.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.498 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I studied microbiology

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:02.135
and the impacts of antioxidants
on model organisms

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:06.072
known as the C. elegans
which is of the nematode family.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's something
you have in common

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.109
with the president, because
I think he did that, too.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:14.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because he's a nematode?
-He's an antioxidant.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.851
Thank you so much for being
here. I really appreciate it.

